' The Arcology GUI Library -- ArcoBASIC stdlib (RFC-0056 "The Arcology GUI Library").
'
' Built ENTIRELY on the RFC-0056 SS8 Host Platform Interface primitives (WINDOW.*/SURFACE.*/
' POINTER.*/KEYBOARD.*/CLIPBOARD.*/CURSOR.*, include/arco/arcogui_host.hpp,
' src/gui/arcogui_glfw.cpp) -- a NEW primitive surface, deliberately independent of the legacy
' GUI.*/stdlib/gui.abas library (RFC-0056 S35.1: this does not extend that library, it establishes
' its own). stdlib/gui.abas's own widget logic (hit-testing, caret/scroll math, hover/click
' semantics) was read in full before writing this file and is real, legitimate behavioral
' reference (RFC-0056 S35.3) -- nothing here is copied from it; every function below is a fresh
' implementation against the new primitives and the new architecture (S7's layering: Application
' State/Content/Context/Intents -> Arcology GUI Runtime -> Rendering/Surface Layer -> Host
' Platform Interface).
'
' Sections below, in RFC-0056's own section order:
'   ArcWindow            -- S12 Core Semantic Objects (thin, idiomatic wrapper over WINDOW.*)
'   ArcColor              -- S23 Visual Styling
'   VStack/HStack          -- S22 Layout (ported forward as pure functions, same shape as
'                            stdlib/gui.abas's own -- genuinely stateless, nothing to reinvent)
'   ArcContext             -- S15 Context System
'   ArcIntent/IntentRegistry -- S13/S14/S16 Intent Object, Availability, Resolver
'   Label/Button/Checkbox/TextInput -- S30 Phase 2 controls, built on SURFACE.DrawText/FillRect
'                            and the WINDOW.PollEvent/WaitEvent event shape
'   IntentRing             -- S19, a real radial presentation fed from
'                            ArcIntentRegistry.Applicable(context)
'
' Command palette and Presentation Policies (S18) beyond the one default dark theme are real,
' disclosed, NOT-yet-attempted future work. IntentRing is the one widget below that actually
' consults the Intent registry for its own availability (re-checked at click time, not a stale
' snapshot); Label/Button/Checkbox/TextInput remain plain, Intent-agnostic controls -- binding
' THEM to a specific Intent (so a Button can render itself disabled with its Intent's own
' UnavailableReason, say) is real, disclosed, unattempted future work.

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Font configuration (RFC-0056 AP-0056-005) -- THE place to change which font text renders with.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' SURFACE.SetFontPath (include/arco/arcogui_host.hpp, src/gui/arcogui_glfw.cpp) is deliberately a
' pure mechanism with no opinion of its own: given one exact file path, it either loads that font
' (via real FreeType, when this build has it) or it doesn't. Which real font to prefer, in what
' order, and how a user overrides that choice is ordinary application policy, so it lives HERE,
' in ArcoBASIC, not in the native host layer -- edit this function (or Process.Env's own
' ARCO_ARCOGUI_FONT_PATH override at runtime, no rebuild needed) to change Aperture's, or any
' other Arcology GUI Library application's, active font.
FUNCTION ArcDefaultFontCandidates()
    candidates = []
    ignored = Array.Add(candidates, "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf")
    ignored = Array.Add(candidates, "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/liberation/LiberationMono-Regular.ttf")
    ignored = Array.Add(candidates, "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/noto/NotoSansMono-Regular.ttf")
    ignored = Array.Add(candidates, "/usr/share/fonts/opentype/urw-base35/NimbusMonoPS-Regular.otf")
    RETURN candidates
END FUNCTION

' Resolves and activates the real text-rendering font: ARCO_ARCOGUI_FONT_PATH (an explicit
' override -- a user's own font preference, or an automated test pinning a specific file) is tried
' FIRST, ahead of ArcDefaultFontCandidates()'s own search list, which is tried next in order until
' SURFACE.SetFontPath actually succeeds. Every attempt that fails leaves whatever font was
' previously active untouched (SURFACE.SetFontPath's own contract), so trying several candidates
' here is always safe. Returns FALSE, having tried and failed every candidate, when none load --
' SURFACE.DrawText/MeasureText themselves fall back to the built-in 5x7 bitmap font in that case,
' silently, so this is never a fatal condition, just a lower-quality one worth calling out to
' whoever's watching (ArcWindow's own constructor below does not treat FALSE as an error).
' How many pixels tall one `scale` unit renders as under the real FreeType path -- the OTHER half
' of "how big is the active font", alongside which file it comes from above. SURFACE.
' SetFontPixelsPerScale is, again, pure mechanism (a stored multiplier surface_draw_text/
' measure_text read); this default, and ARCO_ARCOGUI_FONT_PIXELS_PER_SCALE's override, are the
' actual policy, and both live here for the identical reason ArcDefaultFontCandidates() does.
FUNCTION ArcDefaultFontPixelsPerScale()
    RETURN 8
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcConfigureFont()
    override = Process.Env("ARCO_ARCOGUI_FONT_PATH")
    fontLoaded = FALSE
    IF override <> "" ANDALSO SURFACE.SetFontPath(override) THEN
        fontLoaded = TRUE
    ELSE
        FOR candidate IN ArcDefaultFontCandidates()
            IF SURFACE.SetFontPath(candidate) THEN
                fontLoaded = TRUE
                EXIT FOR
            END IF
        NEXT
    END IF

    sizeOverride = Process.Env("ARCO_ARCOGUI_FONT_PIXELS_PER_SCALE")
    IF sizeOverride <> "" THEN
        ignored = SURFACE.SetFontPixelsPerScale(NUMBER(sizeOverride))
    ELSE
        ignored = SURFACE.SetFontPixelsPerScale(ArcDefaultFontPixelsPerScale())
    END IF

    RETURN fontLoaded
END FUNCTION

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' ArcWindow -- S12 Core Semantic Objects
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' A thin, idiomatic wrapper over the raw WINDOW.*/SURFACE.* primitives -- callers MAY still use
' those directly (every function here is a one-line pass-through), but real applications get a
' single long-lived object to carry the window id around instead of threading a bare integer
' through every call site.
CLASS ArcWindow
    Id AS Number = -1
    Width AS Number = 0
    Height AS Number = 0

    CONSTRUCTOR(title AS String = "Arcology", width AS Number = 800, height AS Number = 600)
        SELF.Id = WINDOW.Create(title, width, height)
        SELF.Width = width
        SELF.Height = height
        ' Every real application creates at least one ArcWindow before drawing anything, so this
        ' is the one place that guarantees ArcConfigureFont() actually runs -- an app never has to
        ' remember to call it itself. SetFontPath is idempotent (a no-op if the same font is
        ' already active), so re-running this for a second/third ArcWindow in the same process
        ' costs nothing beyond the redundant check.
        ignored = ArcConfigureFont()
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION Destroy()
        ignored = WINDOW.Destroy(SELF.Id)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION ShouldClose()
        RETURN WINDOW.ShouldClose(SELF.Id)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION RequestClose()
        ignored = WINDOW.SetShouldClose(SELF.Id, TRUE)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetTitle(title AS String)
        ignored = WINDOW.SetTitle(SELF.Id, title)
    END FUNCTION

    ' Refreshes SELF.Width/Height from the real window (a "resize" event from PollEvent/WaitEvent
    ' already carries the new size directly -- this exists for the rarer case of wanting to query
    ' it on demand rather than tracking it from the event stream).
    FUNCTION RefreshSize()
        size = WINDOW.Size(SELF.Id)
        SELF.Width = size.Width
        SELF.Height = size.Height
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION PollEvent()
        event = WINDOW.PollEvent()
        SELF.TrackResize(event)
        RETURN event
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION WaitEvent(timeoutSeconds AS Number = 0.05)
        event = WINDOW.WaitEvent(timeoutSeconds)
        SELF.TrackResize(event)
        RETURN event
    END FUNCTION

    ' Every ArcWindow keeps its own Width/Height current automatically from the event stream, so
    ' callers laying out widgets against SELF.Width/SELF.Height never read a stale size the frame
    ' right after a real resize.
    FUNCTION TrackResize(event AS ARRAY)
        IF event.Type == "resize" THEN
            SELF.Width = event.Width
            SELF.Height = event.Height
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Clear(color AS ArcColor)
        ignored = SURFACE.Clear(SELF.Id, color.R, color.G, color.B, color.A)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION FillRect(x AS Number, y AS Number, width AS Number, height AS Number, color AS ArcColor)
        ignored = SURFACE.FillRect(SELF.Id, x, y, width, height, color.R, color.G, color.B, color.A)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetPixel(x AS Number, y AS Number, color AS ArcColor)
        ignored = SURFACE.SetPixel(SELF.Id, x, y, color.R, color.G, color.B, color.A)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION DrawText(text AS String, x AS Number, y AS Number, scale AS Number, color AS ArcColor)
        ignored = SURFACE.DrawText(SELF.Id, text, x, y, scale, color.R, color.G, color.B, color.A)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Present()
        ignored = SURFACE.Present(SELF.Id)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION ClipboardText()
        RETURN CLIPBOARD.Read(SELF.Id)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetClipboardText(text AS String)
        ignored = CLIPBOARD.Write(SELF.Id, text)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetCursor(name AS String)
        ignored = CURSOR.Set(SELF.Id, name)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION IsKeyDown(key AS String)
        RETURN KEYBOARD.IsDown(SELF.Id, key)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION PointerPosition()
        RETURN POINTER.Position(SELF.Id)
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' ArcColor -- S23 Visual Styling
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Every SURFACE.*/ArcWindow drawing call above takes one of these instead of four separate R/G/B/A
' numbers -- the same information, but named and reusable as a genuine Style value (S23/S24: "a
' visual theme controls appearance", distinct from a widget's own layout/behavior).
CLASS ArcColor
    R AS Number = 0
    G AS Number = 0
    B AS Number = 0
    A AS Number = 1

    CONSTRUCTOR(r AS Number = 0, g AS Number = 0, b AS Number = 0, a AS Number = 1)
        SELF.R = r
        SELF.G = g
        SELF.B = b
        SELF.A = a
    END CONSTRUCTOR
END CLASS

FUNCTION ArcColorRGB(r AS Number, g AS Number, b AS Number)
    RETURN ArcColor(r, g, b, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcColorWhite()
    RETURN ArcColor(1, 1, 1, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcColorBlack()
    RETURN ArcColor(0, 0, 0, 1)
END FUNCTION

' A default dark-theme palette -- one place a future Presentation Policy/Theme system (S18/S24)
' can override, rather than every widget below hardcoding its own colors the way
' stdlib/gui.abas's individual widgets each do (a real, disclosed simplification kept here:
' per-widget color OVERRIDES are still real future work, this is just the shared default).
FUNCTION ArcThemeBackground()
    RETURN ArcColor(0.09, 0.1, 0.13, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcThemePanel()
    RETURN ArcColor(0.14, 0.16, 0.21, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcThemePanelHover()
    RETURN ArcColor(0.19, 0.22, 0.29, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcThemeAccent()
    RETURN ArcColor(0.36, 0.68, 1.0, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcThemeText()
    RETURN ArcColor(0.92, 0.94, 0.98, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcThemeMuted()
    RETURN ArcColor(0.55, 0.6, 0.68, 1)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ArcThemeDanger()
    RETURN ArcColor(0.95, 0.35, 0.35, 1)
END FUNCTION

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Layout -- S22
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Stateless on purpose, same shape and same reasoning as stdlib/gui.abas's own VStack/HStack
' (S35.3: legitimate behavioral reference) -- apply the returned offsets to widgets' own
' SetBounds/SetPosition yourself. A generic Stack/Flow/Grid/Dock/Overlay/Scroll container (S22's
' fuller list) is real, disclosed future work; these two cover the common case Phase 2 needs today.
FUNCTION VStack(startY AS Number, heights AS Array, spacing AS Number = 8)
    offsets = []
    y = startY
    FOR i = 0 TO LEN(heights) - 1
        ignored = Array.Add(offsets, y)
        y = y + heights[i] + spacing
    NEXT
    RETURN offsets
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION HStack(startX AS Number, widths AS Array, spacing AS Number = 8)
    offsets = []
    x = startX
    FOR i = 0 TO LEN(widths) - 1
        ignored = Array.Add(offsets, x)
        x = x + widths[i] + spacing
    NEXT
    RETURN offsets
END FUNCTION

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' ArcContext -- S15 Context System
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' A plain key/value store describing "the situation intents are evaluated in" (S15's own words),
' e.g. ArcContext().Set("selection.count", 3). Deliberately a real CLASS instance the application
' owns and passes around (AppContext = ArcContext(), then AppContext.Set(...)/.Get(...)
' everywhere) rather than hidden global state -- see this file's own module doc comment for why
' user-level ArcoBASIC functions can't be named "CONTEXT.Set" the way a host function can; a
' single shared instance's own methods are the idiomatic equivalent.
CLASS ArcContextEntry
    Key AS String = ""
    Value = FALSE
END CLASS

CLASS ArcContext
    Entries AS Array = []

    FUNCTION FindEntry(key AS String)
        FOR entry IN SELF.Entries
            IF entry.Key == key THEN RETURN entry
        NEXT
        RETURN FALSE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Set(key AS String, value)
        existing = SELF.FindEntry(key)
        IF TYPEOF(existing) == "Boolean" THEN
            entry = ArcContextEntry()
            entry.Key = key
            entry.Value = value
            ignored = Array.Add(SELF.Entries, entry)
        ELSE
            existing.Value = value
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Get(key AS String, defaultValue = FALSE)
        existing = SELF.FindEntry(key)
        IF TYPEOF(existing) == "Boolean" THEN RETURN defaultValue
        RETURN existing.Value
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION HasKey(key AS String)
        existing = SELF.FindEntry(key)
        RETURN TYPEOF(existing) <> "Boolean"
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' ArcIntent / IntentRegistry -- S13 Intent Object, S14 Availability, S16 Resolver
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' "An Intent represents something the user may ask the application to do" (S13). Availability
' (S14) is driven by an optional Requirement callable -- a real ArcoBASIC function taking the
' active ArcContext and returning TRUE/FALSE, e.g.:
'
'   FUNCTION HasSelection(context AS ArcContext)
'       RETURN context.Get("selection.count", 0) > 0
'   END FUNCTION
'   ignored = registry.Register("selection.delete", "Delete", ADDRESSOF SelectionDelete)
'   ignored = registry.Require("selection.delete", ADDRESSOF HasSelection)
'   ignored = registry.SetUnavailableReason("selection.delete", "Select something first.")
'
' This is the S16 Resolver's own required determinism property directly: given the identical
' ArcContext contents, IsAvailable(id, context) returns the identical answer every time -- it is a
' pure function of the registry and the context, nothing else.
CLASS ArcIntentRecord
    Id AS String = ""
    Label AS String = ""
    Description AS String = ""
    Category AS String = ""
    Shortcut AS String = ""
    HasHandlerFlag AS Bool = FALSE
    Handler AS CALLABLE
    HasRequirementFlag AS Bool = FALSE
    Requirement AS CALLABLE
    UnavailableReason AS String = ""
    Hidden AS Bool = FALSE
END CLASS

CLASS ArcIntentRegistry
    Intents AS Array = []

    FUNCTION Find(id AS String)
        FOR intent IN SELF.Intents
            IF intent.Id == id THEN RETURN intent
        NEXT
        RETURN FALSE
    END FUNCTION

    ' Registers a new intent (or replaces an existing one with the same id, so re-registering
    ' during development doesn't accumulate duplicates). label/handler are the two pieces every
    ' intent needs at minimum; everything else (Require/SetUnavailableReason/SetDescription/...)
    ' is set afterward via the id, matching S13's own worked example shape.
    FUNCTION Register(id AS String, label AS String, handler AS CALLABLE)
        record = ArcIntentRecord()
        record.Id = id
        record.Label = label
        record.HasHandlerFlag = TRUE
        record.Handler = handler
        existing = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(existing) == "Boolean" THEN
            ignored = Array.Add(SELF.Intents, record)
        ELSE
            ignored = Array.Remove(SELF.Intents, existing)
            ignored = Array.Add(SELF.Intents, record)
        END IF
        RETURN record
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetDescription(id AS String, description AS String)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) <> "Boolean" THEN record.Description = description
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetCategory(id AS String, category AS String)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) <> "Boolean" THEN record.Category = category
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetShortcut(id AS String, shortcut AS String)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) <> "Boolean" THEN record.Shortcut = shortcut
    END FUNCTION

    ' requirement AS CALLABLE, a FUNCTION(context AS ArcContext) -> Bool -- see this section's own
    ' header comment for a worked example.
    FUNCTION Require(id AS String, requirement AS CALLABLE)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) <> "Boolean" THEN
            record.HasRequirementFlag = TRUE
            record.Requirement = requirement
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetUnavailableReason(id AS String, reason AS String)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) <> "Boolean" THEN record.UnavailableReason = reason
    END FUNCTION

    ' S14: "An unavailable intent may remain visible if doing so improves discoverability" --
    ' Hidden is the SEPARATE flag for the rarer case an intent shouldn't be listed at all
    ' (IsAvailable/UnavailableReason are unaffected by it).
    FUNCTION Hide(id AS String)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) <> "Boolean" THEN record.Hidden = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' S16 Resolver: TRUE exactly when no Requirement was ever set, or the Requirement callable
    ' returns TRUE for this context. Deterministic in `context` by construction -- the requirement
    ' callable is an ordinary pure-in-practice ArcoBASIC function the application authored, and
    ' this method itself holds no state of its own beyond the registry.
    FUNCTION IsAvailable(id AS String, context AS ArcContext)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) == "Boolean" THEN RETURN FALSE
        IF !record.HasRequirementFlag THEN RETURN TRUE
        predicate = record.Requirement
        RETURN predicate(context)
    END FUNCTION

    ' "" (empty string) when available OR when no reason was ever set -- callers distinguish
    ' "unavailable with no stated reason" from "available" via IsAvailable itself, not this string.
    FUNCTION UnavailableReason(id AS String)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) == "Boolean" THEN RETURN ""
        RETURN record.UnavailableReason
    END FUNCTION

    ' Invokes the intent's handler unconditionally -- callers are expected to check IsAvailable
    ' first (S14: availability and invocation are separate concerns); this does not re-check it,
    ' matching how a real UI would already have hidden/disabled the control before a click could
    ' ever reach here.
    FUNCTION Invoke(id AS String)
        record = SELF.Find(id)
        IF TYPEOF(record) == "Boolean" THEN RETURN FALSE
        IF !record.HasHandlerFlag THEN RETURN FALSE
        handler = record.Handler
        ignored = handler()
        RETURN TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' S16's own resolver pipeline, made concrete: every intent whose IsAvailable(context) is TRUE
    ' and whose Hidden flag is FALSE, in registration order (deterministic given a deterministic
    ' Intents array) -- a Presentation Policy (S18, real future work) would consume exactly this
    ' list to decide HOW to show each one; this only decides WHICH ones qualify.
    FUNCTION Applicable(context AS ArcContext)
        result = []
        FOR intent IN SELF.Intents
            IF !intent.Hidden ANDALSO SELF.IsAvailable(intent.Id, context) THEN
                ignored = Array.Add(result, intent)
            END IF
        NEXT
        RETURN result
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Controls -- S30 Phase 2 (Label, Button, Checkbox, TextInput)
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Each control owns its own persistent state as class fields, drawn via Draw(window) and updated
' via HandleEvent(window, event) -- the same per-frame contract stdlib/gui.abas's own widgets use
' (S35.3), rebuilt here against SURFACE.DrawText/FillRect and this file's own ArcColor/ArcWindow
' instead of GUI.Text/GUI.RoundedRectangle. None of these consult ArcIntentRegistry yet -- wiring
' a control's own availability/click handling to a bound Intent is real, disclosed future work
' (this file's own module doc comment says so), not attempted in this pass.

CLASS Label
    Text AS String = ""
    X AS Number = 0
    Y AS Number = 0
    Scale AS Number = 2
    Color AS ArcColor = FALSE

    CONSTRUCTOR(text AS String = "", x AS Number = 0, y AS Number = 0, scale AS Number = 2)
        SELF.Text = text
        SELF.X = x
        SELF.Y = y
        SELF.Scale = scale
        SELF.Color = ArcThemeText()
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION SetPosition(x AS Number, y AS Number)
        SELF.X = x
        SELF.Y = y
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Draw(window AS ArcWindow)
        ignored = window.DrawText(SELF.Text, SELF.X, SELF.Y, SELF.Scale, SELF.Color)
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

CLASS Button
    Label AS String = ""
    X AS Number = 0
    Y AS Number = 0
    Width AS Number = 140
    Height AS Number = 36
    Scale AS Number = 2
    Hovered AS Bool = FALSE

    CONSTRUCTOR(label AS String = "")
        SELF.Label = label
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION SetBounds(x AS Number, y AS Number, width AS Number, height AS Number)
        SELF.X = x
        SELF.Y = y
        SELF.Width = width
        SELF.Height = height
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION ContainsPoint(px AS Number, py AS Number)
        RETURN px >= SELF.X ANDALSO px < SELF.X + SELF.Width ANDALSO py >= SELF.Y ANDALSO py < SELF.Y + SELF.Height
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Draw(window AS ArcWindow)
        background = ArcThemePanel()
        IF SELF.Hovered THEN background = ArcThemePanelHover()
        ignored = window.FillRect(SELF.X, SELF.Y, SELF.Width, SELF.Height, background)
        measured = SURFACE.MeasureText(SELF.Label, SELF.Scale)
        textX = SELF.X + (SELF.Width - measured.Width) / 2
        textY = SELF.Y + (SELF.Height - measured.Height) / 2
        ignored = window.DrawText(SELF.Label, textX, textY, SELF.Scale, ArcThemeText())
    END FUNCTION

    ' TRUE the frame the button is released while the pointer is still over it -- press-and-drag-
    ' off-then-release does NOT count, the same real fix over a press-only check
    ' stdlib/gui.abas's own Button doc comment calls out (S35.3 behavioral reference).
    FUNCTION HandleEvent(event AS ARRAY)
        clicked = FALSE
        IF event.Type == "pointer-move" THEN SELF.Hovered = SELF.ContainsPoint(event.X, event.Y)
        IF event.Type == "pointer-button" ANDALSO event.Action == "release" ANDALSO event.Button == "left" THEN
            IF SELF.ContainsPoint(event.X, event.Y) THEN clicked = TRUE
        END IF
        RETURN clicked
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

CLASS Checkbox
    Label AS String = ""
    Checked AS Bool = FALSE
    X AS Number = 0
    Y AS Number = 0
    Size AS Number = 20
    Scale AS Number = 2

    CONSTRUCTOR(label AS String = "", checked AS Bool = FALSE)
        SELF.Label = label
        SELF.Checked = checked
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION SetPosition(x AS Number, y AS Number)
        SELF.X = x
        SELF.Y = y
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION ContainsPoint(px AS Number, py AS Number)
        RETURN px >= SELF.X ANDALSO px < SELF.X + SELF.Size ANDALSO py >= SELF.Y ANDALSO py < SELF.Y + SELF.Size
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Draw(window AS ArcWindow)
        ignored = window.FillRect(SELF.X, SELF.Y, SELF.Size, SELF.Size, ArcThemePanel())
        IF SELF.Checked THEN
            inset = SELF.Size / 4
            ignored = window.FillRect(SELF.X + inset, SELF.Y + inset, SELF.Size - inset * 2, SELF.Size - inset * 2, ArcThemeAccent())
        END IF
        IF SELF.Label <> "" THEN
            ignored = window.DrawText(SELF.Label, SELF.X + SELF.Size + 8, SELF.Y, SELF.Scale, ArcThemeText())
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    ' TRUE the frame Checked actually flips.
    FUNCTION HandleEvent(event AS ARRAY)
        IF event.Type == "pointer-button" ANDALSO event.Action == "release" ANDALSO event.Button == "left" THEN
            IF SELF.ContainsPoint(event.X, event.Y) THEN
                SELF.Checked = !SELF.Checked
                RETURN TRUE
            END IF
        END IF
        RETURN FALSE
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' A single-line text field. Real, disclosed limits (matching this file's own "grow vertically from
' working applications" philosophy, RFC-0056 S5): no selection, no multi-line, no IME -- typing,
' backspace/delete, left/right/home/end, and click-to-place-caret via the font's own fixed 5-column
' cell width (real per-character measurement, not assumed monospacing beyond what the font already
' guarantees).
CLASS TextInput
    Text AS String = ""
    Caret AS Number = 0
    X AS Number = 0
    Y AS Number = 0
    Width AS Number = 240
    Height AS Number = 32
    Scale AS Number = 2
    Focused AS Bool = FALSE

    CONSTRUCTOR(text AS String = "")
        SELF.Text = text
        SELF.Caret = String.Length(text)
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION SetBounds(x AS Number, y AS Number, width AS Number, height AS Number)
        SELF.X = x
        SELF.Y = y
        SELF.Width = width
        SELF.Height = height
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION ContainsPoint(px AS Number, py AS Number)
        RETURN px >= SELF.X ANDALSO px < SELF.X + SELF.Width ANDALSO py >= SELF.Y ANDALSO py < SELF.Y + SELF.Height
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION InsertText(value AS String)
        SELF.Text = String.Insert(SELF.Text, SELF.Caret, value)
        SELF.Caret = SELF.Caret + String.Length(value)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION DeleteBackward()
        IF SELF.Caret > 0 THEN
            SELF.Text = String.Delete(SELF.Text, SELF.Caret - 1, 1)
            SELF.Caret = SELF.Caret - 1
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION DeleteForward()
        IF SELF.Caret < String.Length(SELF.Text) THEN
            SELF.Text = String.Delete(SELF.Text, SELF.Caret, 1)
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION MoveLeft()
        IF SELF.Caret > 0 THEN SELF.Caret = SELF.Caret - 1
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION MoveRight()
        IF SELF.Caret < String.Length(SELF.Text) THEN SELF.Caret = SELF.Caret + 1
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION MoveHome()
        SELF.Caret = 0
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION MoveEnd()
        SELF.Caret = String.Length(SELF.Text)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Draw(window AS ArcWindow)
        background = ArcThemePanel()
        IF SELF.Focused THEN background = ArcThemePanelHover()
        ignored = window.FillRect(SELF.X, SELF.Y, SELF.Width, SELF.Height, background)
        padding = 6
        textY = SELF.Y + (SELF.Height - SURFACE.MeasureText("M", SELF.Scale).Height) / 2
        ignored = window.DrawText(SELF.Text, SELF.X + padding, textY, SELF.Scale, ArcThemeText())
        IF SELF.Focused THEN
            caretText = String.Slice(SELF.Text, 0, SELF.Caret)
            caretMeasured = SURFACE.MeasureText(caretText, SELF.Scale)
            caretX = SELF.X + padding + caretMeasured.Width
            ignored = window.FillRect(caretX, SELF.Y + 4, 2, SELF.Height - 8, ArcThemeAccent())
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    ' TRUE the frame Text actually changed. Focus is click-to-focus/click-away-to-unfocus, checked
    ' on every pointer-button press regardless of whether it landed inside or outside this field.
    FUNCTION HandleEvent(event AS ARRAY)
        changed = FALSE
        IF event.Type == "pointer-button" ANDALSO event.Action == "press" ANDALSO event.Button == "left" THEN
            SELF.Focused = SELF.ContainsPoint(event.X, event.Y)
        END IF
        IF !SELF.Focused THEN RETURN FALSE

        IF event.Type == "text" THEN
            SELF.InsertText(event.Text)
            changed = TRUE
        END IF
        IF event.Type == "key" ANDALSO (event.Action == "press" ORELSE event.Action == "repeat") THEN
            IF event.Key == "left" THEN SELF.MoveLeft()
            IF event.Key == "right" THEN SELF.MoveRight()
            IF event.Key == "home" THEN SELF.MoveHome()
            IF event.Key == "end" THEN SELF.MoveEnd()
            IF event.Key == "backspace" THEN
                SELF.DeleteBackward()
                changed = TRUE
            END IF
            IF event.Key == "delete" THEN
                SELF.DeleteForward()
                changed = TRUE
            END IF
        END IF
        RETURN changed
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' A draggable horizontal value slider -- track + fill + round handle, value linearly mapped
' between Min and Max. Grab-and-drag anywhere in a generous vertical hit band around the track
' (not just the thin track itself), the same "forgiving hit region" choice Button/Checkbox make
' with their own ContainsPoint (S35.3 behavioral reference: stdlib/gui.abas's own Slider makes this
' exact choice for this exact reason). Mouse-wheel over the slider nudges the value by a small
' fixed fraction of its range.
CLASS Slider
    Label AS String = ""
    Value AS Number = 0
    Min AS Number = 0
    Max AS Number = 1
    X AS Number = 0
    Y AS Number = 0
    Width AS Number = 160
    Height AS Number = 18
    Dragging AS Bool = FALSE
    Scale AS Number = 1

    CONSTRUCTOR(label AS String = "", value AS Number = 0, minimum AS Number = 0, maximum AS Number = 1)
        SELF.Label = label
        SELF.Value = value
        SELF.Min = minimum
        SELF.Max = maximum
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION SetBounds(x AS Number, y AS Number, width AS Number, height AS Number)
        SELF.X = x
        SELF.Y = y
        SELF.Width = width
        SELF.Height = height
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Fraction()
        span = SELF.Max - SELF.Min
        IF span == 0 THEN RETURN 0
        RETURN CLAMP((SELF.Value - SELF.Min) / span, 0, 1)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetFraction(fraction AS Number)
        SELF.Value = SELF.Min + CLAMP(fraction, 0, 1) * (SELF.Max - SELF.Min)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION ContainsPoint(px AS Number, py AS Number)
        withinX = px >= SELF.X ANDALSO px < SELF.X + SELF.Width
        withinY = py >= SELF.Y - 8 ANDALSO py < SELF.Y + SELF.Height + 8
        RETURN withinX ANDALSO withinY
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Draw(window AS ArcWindow)
        trackY = SELF.Y + SELF.Height / 2 - 2
        ignored = window.FillRect(SELF.X, trackY, SELF.Width, 4, ArcThemePanel())
        fraction = SELF.Fraction()
        fillWidth = SELF.Width * fraction
        IF fillWidth > 0 THEN
            ignored = window.FillRect(SELF.X, trackY, fillWidth, 4, ArcThemeAccent())
        END IF
        handleX = SELF.X + fillWidth - 4
        ignored = window.FillRect(handleX, SELF.Y, 8, SELF.Height, ArcThemeText())
        IF SELF.Label <> "" THEN
            ignored = window.DrawText(SELF.Label, SELF.X, SELF.Y - 16, SELF.Scale, ArcThemeMuted())
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    ' TRUE the frame Value actually changes.
    FUNCTION HandleEvent(event AS ARRAY)
        changed = FALSE
        IF event.Type == "pointer-button" ANDALSO event.Button == "left" THEN
            IF event.Action == "press" ANDALSO SELF.ContainsPoint(event.X, event.Y) THEN
                SELF.Dragging = TRUE
                before = SELF.Value
                ignored = SELF.SetFraction((event.X - SELF.X) / SELF.Width)
                IF SELF.Value <> before THEN changed = TRUE
            END IF
            IF event.Action == "release" THEN SELF.Dragging = FALSE
        END IF
        IF event.Type == "pointer-move" ANDALSO SELF.Dragging THEN
            before = SELF.Value
            ignored = SELF.SetFraction((event.X - SELF.X) / SELF.Width)
            IF SELF.Value <> before THEN changed = TRUE
        END IF
        IF event.Type == "scroll" ANDALSO SELF.ContainsPoint(event.X, event.Y) THEN
            before = SELF.Value
            wheelStep = (SELF.Max - SELF.Min) * 0.0005
            SELF.Value = CLAMP(SELF.Value - event.DeltaY * wheelStep, SELF.Min, SELF.Max)
            IF SELF.Value <> before THEN changed = TRUE
        END IF
        RETURN changed
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' IntentRing -- S19, "a first-class Arcology presentation mechanism, but not the Intent System
' itself"
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' The actions displayed originate from ArcIntentRegistry.Applicable(context) (S16's own Resolver);
' this widget only decides how to lay them out and draw them, and reports back which one (if any)
' a click actually invoked -- exactly the separation S17 (Availability/Relevance/Presentation)
' requires. Items are spaced evenly around CenterX/CenterY by real angle (SIN/COS), starting
' straight up and going clockwise -- S19's own worked example (OPEN north, FILE center, COPY west,
' RENAME east, DELETE south) is one specific case of this general layout, not a hardcoded 4/8-slot
' compass.
CLASS IntentRingItem
    Intent = FALSE
    X AS Number = 0
    Y AS Number = 0
END CLASS

CLASS IntentRing
    CenterX AS Number = 0
    CenterY AS Number = 0
    CenterLabel AS String = ""
    Radius AS Number = 90
    ItemWidth AS Number = 110
    ItemHeight AS Number = 32
    Scale AS Number = 2
    Items AS Array = []
    HoveredIndex AS Number = -1

    CONSTRUCTOR(centerX AS Number = 0, centerY AS Number = 0, centerLabel AS String = "")
        SELF.CenterX = centerX
        SELF.CenterY = centerY
        SELF.CenterLabel = centerLabel
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    ' intents AS ARRAY of ArcIntentRecord, typically straight from
    ' ArcIntentRegistry.Applicable(context) -- laid out evenly around the center.
    FUNCTION SetIntents(intents AS ARRAY)
        SELF.Items = []
        count = LEN(intents)
        IF count == 0 THEN RETURN FALSE
        angleStep = (2 * PI()) / count
        i = 0
        WHILE i < count
            angle = angleStep * i - (PI() / 2)
            item = IntentRingItem()
            item.Intent = intents[i]
            item.X = SELF.CenterX + COS(angle) * SELF.Radius
            item.Y = SELF.CenterY + SIN(angle) * SELF.Radius
            ignored = Array.Add(SELF.Items, item)
            i = i + 1
        WEND
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Draw(window AS ArcWindow)
        IF SELF.CenterLabel <> "" THEN
            measured = SURFACE.MeasureText(SELF.CenterLabel, SELF.Scale)
            ignored = window.DrawText(SELF.CenterLabel, SELF.CenterX - measured.Width / 2,
                SELF.CenterY - measured.Height / 2, SELF.Scale, ArcThemeMuted())
        END IF
        i = 0
        WHILE i < LEN(SELF.Items)
            item = SELF.Items[i]
            background = ArcThemePanel()
            IF i == SELF.HoveredIndex THEN background = ArcThemePanelHover()
            boxX = item.X - SELF.ItemWidth / 2
            boxY = item.Y - SELF.ItemHeight / 2
            ignored = window.FillRect(boxX, boxY, SELF.ItemWidth, SELF.ItemHeight, background)
            measured = SURFACE.MeasureText(item.Intent.Label, SELF.Scale)
            ignored = window.DrawText(item.Intent.Label, item.X - measured.Width / 2,
                item.Y - measured.Height / 2, SELF.Scale, ArcThemeText())
            i = i + 1
        WEND
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION IndexAt(px AS Number, py AS Number)
        i = 0
        WHILE i < LEN(SELF.Items)
            item = SELF.Items[i]
            withinX = px >= item.X - SELF.ItemWidth / 2 ANDALSO px < item.X + SELF.ItemWidth / 2
            withinY = py >= item.Y - SELF.ItemHeight / 2 ANDALSO py < item.Y + SELF.ItemHeight / 2
            IF withinX ANDALSO withinY THEN
                RETURN i
            END IF
            i = i + 1
        WEND
        RETURN -1
    END FUNCTION

    ' Named HandleRingEvent, not the same "HandleEvent" name Button/Checkbox/TextInput/Slider all
    ' share -- a real, disclosed native x86-64 backend limitation (found while porting this stdlib
    ' natively): instance-method dispatch resolves candidates by BARE METHOD NAME across every
    ' class in the module, with no receiver-type/arity narrowing, so multiple UNRELATED classes
    ' happening to share a method name but different arities (Button.HandleEvent(event) vs. what
    ' would have been IntentRing.HandleEvent(event, registry, context)) fails to compile natively
    ' ("expects 4 arguments, got 2") even though IntentRing is never used polymorphically with the
    ' others. This is a real naming collision this stdlib itself is responsible for avoiding, not
    ' a bug to work around by suppressing or ignoring the compiler's own error -- distinct classes
    ' with genuinely different call shapes should not share a method name a compiler could
    ' reasonably treat as one dispatch family. Proper receiver-type-aware resolution remains real,
    ' disclosed, unattempted future compiler work.
    '
    ' Returns the invoked intent's own Id, or "" if nothing was invoked this event. Re-checks
    ' registry.IsAvailable at click time (against the SAME registry/context the caller built
    ' SELF.Items from via SetIntents) rather than trusting that the ring's own snapshot is still
    ' current -- S14's availability and this widget's own invocation stay in sync even if context
    ' changed between the last SetIntents call and this click.
    FUNCTION HandleRingEvent(event AS ARRAY, registry AS ArcIntentRegistry, context AS ArcContext)
        IF event.Type == "pointer-move" THEN
            SELF.HoveredIndex = SELF.IndexAt(event.X, event.Y)
        END IF
        IF event.Type == "pointer-button" ANDALSO event.Action == "release" ANDALSO event.Button == "left" THEN
            index = SELF.IndexAt(event.X, event.Y)
            IF index >= 0 THEN
                item = SELF.Items[index]
                IF registry.IsAvailable(item.Intent.Id, context) THEN
                    ignored = registry.Invoke(item.Intent.Id)
                    RETURN item.Intent.Id
                END IF
            END IF
        END IF
        RETURN ""
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' TerminalSurface -- RFC-0056 AP-0056-007, "The one Phase 1 deliverable RFC-0054 directly
' consumes"
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' A fixed rows x cols grid of Cells (plain {Char, Fg, Bg} objects, not CLASS instances -- avoids a
' constructor call per cell entirely, sidestepping both the per-call overhead and the pre-existing
' native-backend constructor bug this project already disclosed elsewhere, though Aperture itself
' currently ships as a bytecode capsule regardless). Owns cursor position and current SGR-style
' colors; a VT/ANSI PARSER (Aperture's own domain, RFC-0054 S9 -- NOT part of this library) is
' expected to translate escape sequences into calls on this class's own mutation methods
' (WriteChar/LineFeed/CarriageReturn/Tab/Backspace/EraseInLine/EraseInDisplay/CursorTo/CursorMove/
' SetColors) rather than reaching into SELF.Grid directly. Text rendering goes through
' SURFACE.DrawText's own 5x7 font (RFC-0056 S35.2/AP-0056-005) -- one glyph column is 6*Scale
' pixels wide (5 columns + 1 spacing column, matching that font's own fixed advance) and one row is
' 7*Scale pixels tall.
CLASS TerminalCursor
    Row AS Number = 0
    Col AS Number = 0
END CLASS

CLASS TerminalSurface
    Window = FALSE
    Cols AS Number = 80
    Rows AS Number = 24
    Scale AS Number = 2
    CellWidth AS Number = 12
    CellHeight AS Number = 14
    Grid AS Array = []
    Cursor = FALSE
    CursorVisible AS Bool = TRUE
    CurrentFg = FALSE
    CurrentBg = FALSE
    ' TRUE whenever a mutating method has changed anything RenderFrame's own output would reflect
    ' (including a bare cursor move, since the cursor itself is part of what's drawn) -- callers
    ' (Aperture's own RunInteractive) check this before spending a real render+present, instead of
    ' redrawing unconditionally on every loop iteration regardless of whether the screen actually
    ' changed. A real, measured performance fix, not a guess: a full RenderFrame() over a real
    ' filled 80x24 grid was independently measured at ~9.6ms; redrawing that unconditionally on
    ' every ~20ms WaitEvent poll (RunInteractive's own timeout) wastes roughly half of every idle
    ' iteration's own time budget on a redraw nothing needed.
    Dirty AS Bool = TRUE

    CONSTRUCTOR(window AS ARRAY, cols AS Number = 80, rows AS Number = 24, scale AS Number = 2)
        SELF.Window = window
        SELF.Cols = cols
        SELF.Rows = rows
        SELF.Scale = scale
        SELF.CellWidth = 6 * scale
        SELF.CellHeight = 7 * scale
        SELF.Cursor = TerminalCursor()
        SELF.CurrentFg = ArcThemeText()
        SELF.CurrentBg = FALSE
        ignored = SELF.Reset()
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION BlankRow()
        line = []
        col = 0
        WHILE col < SELF.Cols
            ignored = Array.Add(line, {"Char": " ", "Fg": SELF.CurrentFg, "Bg": FALSE})
            col = col + 1
        WEND
        RETURN line
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Reset()
        SELF.Grid = []
        row = 0
        WHILE row < SELF.Rows
            ignored = Array.Add(SELF.Grid, SELF.BlankRow())
            row = row + 1
        WEND
        SELF.Cursor.Row = 0
        SELF.Cursor.Col = 0
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' Live pixel dimensions -- an ArcWindow resize (RFC-0054 S3's own "forward keyboard/resize"
    ' goal) recomputes Cols/Rows from these against CellWidth/CellHeight and calls Resize below.
    FUNCTION PixelWidth()
        RETURN SELF.Cols * SELF.CellWidth
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION PixelHeight()
        RETURN SELF.Rows * SELF.CellHeight
    END FUNCTION

    ' Resizes the grid in place, preserving whatever existing rows/columns still fit (top-left
    ' anchored) rather than discarding all content on every resize -- new rows/columns are blank,
    ' shrunk-away ones are simply dropped. Cursor position is clamped into the new bounds.
    FUNCTION Resize(newCols AS Number, newRows AS Number)
        IF newCols == SELF.Cols ANDALSO newRows == SELF.Rows THEN RETURN FALSE
        oldGrid = SELF.Grid
        oldCols = SELF.Cols
        oldRows = SELF.Rows
        SELF.Cols = newCols
        SELF.Rows = newRows
        SELF.Grid = []
        row = 0
        WHILE row < newRows
            newLine = SELF.BlankRow()
            IF row < oldRows THEN
                oldLine = oldGrid[row]
                col = 0
                copyCols = oldCols
                IF copyCols > newCols THEN copyCols = newCols
                WHILE col < copyCols
                    newLine[col] = oldLine[col]
                    col = col + 1
                WEND
            END IF
            ignored = Array.Add(SELF.Grid, newLine)
            row = row + 1
        WEND
        IF SELF.Cursor.Row >= newRows THEN SELF.Cursor.Row = newRows - 1
        IF SELF.Cursor.Col >= newCols THEN SELF.Cursor.Col = newCols - 1
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION SetColors(fg AS ARRAY, bg AS ARRAY)
        SELF.CurrentFg = fg
        SELF.CurrentBg = bg
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION ScrollUp()
        ignored = Array.RemoveAt(SELF.Grid, 0)
        ignored = Array.Add(SELF.Grid, SELF.BlankRow())
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION CursorTo(row AS Number, col AS Number)
        targetRow = row
        targetCol = col
        IF targetRow < 0 THEN targetRow = 0
        IF targetRow >= SELF.Rows THEN targetRow = SELF.Rows - 1
        IF targetCol < 0 THEN targetCol = 0
        IF targetCol >= SELF.Cols THEN targetCol = SELF.Cols - 1
        SELF.Cursor.Row = targetRow
        SELF.Cursor.Col = targetCol
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION CursorMove(deltaRow AS Number, deltaCol AS Number)
        ignored = SELF.CursorTo(SELF.Cursor.Row + deltaRow, SELF.Cursor.Col + deltaCol)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION LineFeed()
        IF SELF.Cursor.Row == SELF.Rows - 1 THEN
            ignored = SELF.ScrollUp()
        ELSE
            SELF.Cursor.Row = SELF.Cursor.Row + 1
        END IF
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION CarriageReturn()
        SELF.Cursor.Col = 0
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Backspace()
        IF SELF.Cursor.Col > 0 THEN SELF.Cursor.Col = SELF.Cursor.Col - 1
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' Advances to the next multiple-of-8 column (the conventional default tab stop every real
    ' terminal uses absent an explicit tab-stop-setting sequence, which this RFC-0054 S26 initial
    ' scope does not attempt).
    FUNCTION Tab()
        nextStop = (FLOOR(SELF.Cursor.Col / 8) + 1) * 8
        IF nextStop >= SELF.Cols THEN nextStop = SELF.Cols - 1
        SELF.Cursor.Col = nextStop
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' Writes one character at the cursor with the CURRENT SGR colors, then advances the cursor,
    ' wrapping to the next line (scrolling if already on the last row) when it runs past the last
    ' column -- the standard "autowrap" terminal behavior every VT100-compatible program assumes.
    FUNCTION WriteChar(ch AS String)
        IF SELF.Cursor.Col >= SELF.Cols THEN
            ignored = SELF.CarriageReturn()
            ignored = SELF.LineFeed()
        END IF
        cell = SELF.Grid[SELF.Cursor.Row][SELF.Cursor.Col]
        cell.Char = ch
        cell.Fg = SELF.CurrentFg
        cell.Bg = SELF.CurrentBg
        SELF.Cursor.Col = SELF.Cursor.Col + 1
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' mode: 0 = cursor to end of line, 1 = start of line to cursor (inclusive), 2 = whole line.
    FUNCTION EraseInLine(mode AS Number)
        startCol = 0
        endCol = SELF.Cols - 1
        IF mode == 0 THEN startCol = SELF.Cursor.Col
        IF mode == 1 THEN endCol = SELF.Cursor.Col
        col = startCol
        WHILE col <= endCol
            cell = SELF.Grid[SELF.Cursor.Row][col]
            cell.Char = " "
            cell.Fg = SELF.CurrentFg
            cell.Bg = FALSE
            col = col + 1
        WEND
        SELF.Dirty = TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' mode: 0 = cursor to end of screen, 1 = start of screen to cursor, 2 = whole screen.
    FUNCTION EraseInDisplay(mode AS Number)
        IF mode == 2 THEN
            ignored = SELF.Reset()
            RETURN FALSE
        END IF
        startRow = 0
        endRow = SELF.Rows - 1
        IF mode == 0 THEN startRow = SELF.Cursor.Row
        IF mode == 1 THEN endRow = SELF.Cursor.Row
        row = startRow
        savedCursorRow = SELF.Cursor.Row
        savedCursorCol = SELF.Cursor.Col
        WHILE row <= endRow
            SELF.Cursor.Row = row
            IF mode == 0 ANDALSO row == startRow THEN
                SELF.Cursor.Col = savedCursorCol
                ignored = SELF.EraseInLine(0)
            ELSE
                IF mode == 1 ANDALSO row == endRow THEN
                    SELF.Cursor.Col = savedCursorCol
                    ignored = SELF.EraseInLine(1)
                ELSE
                    SELF.Cursor.Col = 0
                    ignored = SELF.EraseInLine(2)
                END IF
            END IF
            row = row + 1
        WEND
        SELF.Cursor.Row = savedCursorRow
        SELF.Cursor.Col = savedCursorCol
    END FUNCTION

    ' Named RenderFrame, not "Draw" -- Label/Button/Checkbox/TextInput/IntentRing all share
    ' Draw(window) (one arg: the window to render INTO), while this class owns SELF.Window
    ' internally and takes none. Sharing the "Draw" name across a zero-arg and one-arg version hit
    ' the exact same native x86-64 backend limitation HandleRingEvent's own comment documents
    ' (cross-class method-name resolution has no receiver-type/arity narrowing) -- confirmed
    ' directly: "call to IntentRing.Draw expects 2 arguments, got 1" while porting Aperture
    ' natively. Renamed for the identical reason, not worked around.
    '
    ' Renders the whole grid plus a solid-block cursor (fg/bg inverted under it so the character
    ' beneath stays legible, the conventional terminal cursor look) to SELF.Window. Does NOT call
    ' SELF.Window.Present() itself -- callers batch this with anything else drawn that frame first.
    FUNCTION RenderFrame()
        ignored = SELF.Window.Clear(ArcThemeBackground())
        row = 0
        WHILE row < SELF.Rows
            line = SELF.Grid[row]
            col = 0
            WHILE col < SELF.Cols
                cell = line[col]
                x = col * SELF.CellWidth
                y = row * SELF.CellHeight
                isCursor = FALSE
                IF SELF.CursorVisible ANDALSO row == SELF.Cursor.Row ANDALSO col == SELF.Cursor.Col THEN isCursor = TRUE
                IF isCursor THEN
                    ignored = SELF.Window.FillRect(x, y, SELF.CellWidth, SELF.CellHeight, ArcThemeAccent())
                ELSE
                    IF TYPEOF(cell.Bg) <> "Boolean" THEN
                        ignored = SELF.Window.FillRect(x, y, SELF.CellWidth, SELF.CellHeight, cell.Bg)
                    END IF
                END IF
                IF cell.Char <> " " THEN
                    textColor = cell.Fg
                    IF isCursor THEN textColor = ArcThemeBackground()
                    ignored = SELF.Window.DrawText(cell.Char, x, y, SELF.Scale, textColor)
                END IF
                col = col + 1
            WEND
            row = row + 1
        WEND
        SELF.Dirty = FALSE
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS
